          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Math of Space: Surface Area and Volume"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.841,
            0.071,
            0.881,
            0.087
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "133"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.11,
            0.881,
            0.168
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "a right circular cone of the same base radius and the same height, the cone has one third the volume of the cylinder. This gives an experimental verification of the formula given above."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.168,
            0.883,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here is another hands-on activity that uses modelling clay (earlier this used to be called ‘plasticine’). Carefully mold the clay into a solid cylinder and measure its radius and height. Then reshape the same portion of clay into identical cones, each having the same radius and the same height as the cylinder. You will find that you are able to make exactly three such cones. This brings out the relationship between the volume of the cylinder and cone quite visibly"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.343,
            0.305,
            0.654,
            0.339
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "V = { \\frac { 1 } { 3 } } \\times { \\mathrm { a r e a ~ o f ~ b a s e } } \\times { \\mathrm { h e i g h t } } ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.34,
            0.883,
            0.417
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The formula for the volume of a cone was first found by the Greek mathematician Archimedes (c. 225 BCE). He also derived formulas for the surface area and volume of a sphere (i.e., ball), which we will study in later sections."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.417,
            0.882,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 3:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A right triangle ABC with sides 5 cm, 12 cm and 13 cm is rotated through "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " about the side with length 12 cm. Find the volume of the solid so obtained."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.48,
            0.604,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The triangle has sides 5 cm, 12 cm, 13 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.504,
            0.881,
            0.546
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5^{2}+12^{2}=25+144=169=13^{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the triangle is a right-angled triangle with perpendicular sides 5 cm and 12 cm and hypotenuse 13 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.549,
            0.884,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The triangle is rotated about the side with length 12 cm. When a right-angled triangle rotates about one of its perpendicular sides, it forms a right circular cone. Here, height of cone h = 12 cm, radius of cone r = 5 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.628,
            0.842,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence, volume of the cone "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\overline{(V)}=\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^{2}h=\\frac{1}{3}\\pi\\times5^{2}\\times12=100\\pi cm^{3}."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.366,
            0.722,
            0.631,
            0.75
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exercise Set 14.3"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.768,
            0.816,
            0.801
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For π, use one of the following approximations: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\pi \\approx \\frac{22}{7}   or   \\pi \\approx 3.14"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.802,
            0.881,
            0.842
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the total surface area of a cone, if its slant height is 21 m and diameter of its base is 24 m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.846,
            0.882,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Find the curved surface area of a right circular cone whose slant height is 10 cm and base radius is 7 cm."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
